// ************** MOS-MUSIC OpenHymnal ABC → JPW-ABC 1.0 **************\n// source = sources/openhymnal/OpenHymnal2014.06.abc\n// match = exact title match from content/production/tune-matching.json\n\n.Title\nTitle = 拥戴我主为王（Crown Him with Many Crowns）\nKeyAndMeters = {1=D,4/4}\nWordsByAndMusicBy = Words: Verses 1, 4, 5, 6 & 9: Matthew Bridges, The Passion of Jesus, 1852.\nverses 2 & 3: Godfrey Thring, Hymns and Sacred Lyrics, 1874.\nMusic: 'Diademata' George J. Elvey, 1868.  Setting: "Appendix to Hymns Ancient and Modern", 1869.\ncopyright: public domain.  This score is a part of the Open Hymnal Project, 2008 Revision.\nExpression = {♩=110}\n\n.Voice\n1 1_ 1_ 3 3 | 6.- 6 | 5 1 4 3 | 2.- 2 | 3 5 6 5 | #4 3_ 2_ 5 1' | 7 1' 6 6 | 5.- 5 | 5 3 2 1 | 6.- 6 | 6 #4 3 2 | 7.- 7 | 1'. 7_ 6 5 | 4 2 3 5 | 4 3 2 2 | 1--- |\n\n.Words\nW1@1,1:\n{Crown} {Him} {with} {man} y {crowns,} {the} {Lamb} {up} {on} {His} {throne.} {Hark!} {How} {the} {heav'n} {ly} {an} {them} / {drowns} {all} {mu} {sic} {but} {its} {own.} A {wake,} {my} {soul,} {and} {sing} {of} {Him} {who} {died} {for} {thee,} {And} {hail} {Him} {as} {thy} {match} {less} {King} {through} {all} e {ter} {ni} {ty.}\n